This src/ directory contains all C++ and CUDA C++ source code for the PSCF 
package.  The subdirectories util, pscf, r1, and rp, each contain source 
code for classes and functions defined in a particular C++ namespace. 
The test subdirectory contains source code for a unit test framework.  
Subdirectories util/ and test/ are maintained as separate github 
repositories that are installed as submodules of the pscfpp git 
repository when the repository is cloned using the --recursive option.

Subdirectories (with corresponding C++ namespace names in parentheses):

  util - general utilities for scientific computation (Util)
  pscf - classes accessible throughout the PSCF package (Pscf)
  r1  - real fields, one-dimensional SCFT (Pscf::R1)
  rp   - SCFT & PS-FTS with real periodic fields (Pscf::Rp)
  test - unit testing framework (base classes)


  Directories r1 and rp are "program level" directories that each
  contain files that are used in only one program. All code in 
  each program-level directory is defined within a corresponding 
  program-level namespace (i.e., Pscf::R1 or Pscf::Rp). By convention, 
  code within one program-level namespace and directory may not include
  header files from a different program-level directory, and may not
  use names defined in a different program-level namespace.  Names of 
  classes and other entitites defined in the util and pscf directories 
  may be used in either namespace level namespace or directory.

Files (maintained in the git repository):

  setopts  - script for managing compile-time options
  makefile - main makefile for in-source compilation (build in src)
  programs.mod - doxygen page for program command-line interfaces
  CONTENTS - this file

Files (created by the configure script):

  config.mk - main configuration file (editable makefile fragment)

